warf, Sir Geoffrey Hudson. [Ch. 35; EEWN 14, 364.5-8]',NULL,NULL),(61,'MAG0061',21,'Quentin Durward / \'His opponent seeing . . . in the swollen ford.\' [4 lines]','--- \n- \"103\"\n- \"164\"\n- \"165\"\n- \"166\"\n',10,42,3,'10 x 8','1831','1831',31,'vol. 31 (frontispiece)','EUL, Corson A.7.a.1829-33/31','','Depicts Quentin Durward at the ford confronting Louis XI and Tristan L\'Hermite, both disguised, the former as Maitre Pierre. [Ch. 2; EEWN 15, 32.14-18]',NULL,'2009-04-10 11:33:37'),(62,'MAG0062',21,'\'The mountain chivalry . . . resigned to him\' [4 lines]','--- \n- \"167\"\n- \"164\"\n- \"240\"\n- \"165\"\n',111,70,3,'8 x 6.5','1831','1831',31,'vol. 31 (title-page vignette)','EUL, Corson A.7.a.1829-33/31','','Depicts Louis XI, seated, being served by Jacqueline (the Countess of Croye) in the inn, with Quentin Durward offering assistance. [Ch. 4; EEWN 15, 50.29-31]',NULL,'2009-08-14 07:49:05'),(63,'MAG0063',21,'Quentin Durward / \'Quentin hastily raised . . . the Countess Isabelle\' [3 lines]','--- - \"164\" - \"167\" - \"168\" - \"88\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\"',59,57,3,'10.5 x 8','1831','1831',31,'vol. 32 (frontispiece)','EUL, Corson A.7.a.1829-33/32','','Depicts Quentin Durward attending to the prostrate figure of Isabelle, Countess de Croye in Schonwaldt Castle, with the Syndic Hermann Pavillon looking on in the background. [Ch. 21; EEWN 15, 230.23-25]',NULL,NULL),(64,'MAG0064',21,'\'At length the speed . . . soon have throttled him.\' [4 lines]','--- - \"169\" - \"26\" - \"170\" - \"50\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\"',58,44,3,'7.5 x 6.5','1831','1831',31,'vol. 32 (title-page vignette)','EUL, Corson A.7.a.1829-33/32','','Depicts Hayraddin, disguised as the herald Rouge Sanglier, being pulled down by pursuing boar-hounds. [Ch. 33; EEWN 15, 365.30-32]',NULL,NULL),(65,'MAG0065',24,'Sir Walter Scott, Bart.','--- \n- \"26\"\n- \"72\"\n- \"84\"\n- \"94\"\n',45,57,3,'10.5 x 8','1832','1832',31,'vol. 33 (frontispiece)','EUL, Corson A.7.a.1829-33/33','','Depicts Scott seated with cane in hand with his dog Bran in the bottom right corner; a view of the Eildon Hills is to the left. Disliking a recent portrait by David Wilkie, Robert Cadell commissioned this portrait in March 1830, planning to have it engraved to accompany a volume of the Magnum Opus edition of the novels. (See Russell, Francis, \'Portraits of Sir Walter Scott\' (London: White Brothers, 1987), Item 55, pp.40-41). Also appears in the Centenary edition of the Waverley Novels: see #CEN0001. (Another engraving of the same portrait, by Henry Robinson, appears as the frontispiece to vol. 1 of the Fisher edition of the Waverley Novels. See #FIS0001). ',NULL,'2009-08-14 07:49:40'),(66,'MAG0066',24,'\'Mr Winterblossom was . . . at the public room.\' [4 lines]','--- - \"171\" - \"172\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\"',60,43,3,'6 x 7.5','1832','1832',31,'vol. 33 (title-page vignette)','EUL, Corson A.7.a.1829-33/33','','Depicts Mr Philip Winterblossom, as a man of taste, exhibiting pieces of artwork to others assembled in the public room at Saint Ronan\'s Well. [Ch. 3; EEWN 16, 30.2-4]',NULL,NULL),(67,'MAG0067',24,'St. Ronan\'s Well / \'The minister of St. Ronan\'s . . . to announce his presence.\' [5 lines]','--- \n- \"163\"\n- \"173\"\n- \"175\"\n- \"174\"\n',69,44,3,'9.5 x 8','1832','1832',31,'vol. 34 (frontispiece)','EUL, Corson A.7.a.1829-33/34','','Depicts Mr Touchwood, cane in hand, disturbing the Rev. Josiah Cargill, the latter studying a large folio book [Ch. 17; EEWN 16, 154.19-23]. Exhibited at Royal Academy in 1832, no. 139.',NULL,'2009-06-25 15:08:41'),(68,'MAG0068',24,'\'Slowly and with a feeble hand . . . by the bedside.\' [3 lines]','--- - \"173\" - \"176\" - \"177\" - \"175\" - \"163\" - \"178\" - \"88\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\"',109,16,3,'8.5 x 7.5','1832','1832',31,'vol. 34 (title-page vignette)','EUL, Corson A.7.a.1829-33/34','','Depicts the dying Hannah Irwin, attended by the Rev. Cargill, with the appearance of Clara Mowbray at the bedside. [Ch. 38; EEWN 16, 365.3-7]',NULL,NULL),(69,'MAG0069',22,'Redgauntlet.','--- \n- \"26\"\n- \"67\"\n- \"181\"\n- \"180\"\n- \"183\"\n- \"182\"\n- \"179\"\n',41,70,3,'7.5 x 10','1832','1832',31,'vol. 35 (frontispiece)','EUL, Corson A.7.a.1829-33/35','','Depicts Redgauntlet (\'Herries of Birrenswork\') at supper alongside Darsie Latimer, with Cristal Nixon and Mabel Moffat also at the table, and Greenmantle (Lilias Redgauntlet) saying grace [Letter 4; EEWN 17, 29].',NULL,'2009-06-25 15:10:08'),(70,'MAG0070',22,'\'I was induced . . . with my own hand.\' [4 lines]','--- - \"180\" - \"305\" - \"29\" - \"17\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\"',54,44,3,'7.5 x 6','1832','1832',31,'vol. 35 (title-page vignette)','EUL, Corson A.7.a.1829-33/35','','Depicts Darsie Latimer, having handed over fishing-rod to watching young cowherd (Benjie). [Letter 3; EEWN 17, 18.32-35]',NULL,NULL),(71,'MAG0071',22,'Redgauntlet / \'Are you come light-handed . . . that does something clever.\' [4 lines]','--- \n- \"172\"\n- \"19\"\n- \"186\"\n- \"69\"\n- \"74\"\n- \"185\"\n- \"184\"\n',52,38,3,'10.5 x 7.5','1832','1832',31,'vol. 36 (frontispiece)','EUL, Corson A.7.a.1829-33/36','','Depicts Steenie Steenson, bagpipes under his arm, presenting bag of money as rent to Sir Robert Redgauntlet, with Dougal MacCallum in attendance [Letter 11; EEWN 17.90.1-5]. Exhibited Royal Scottish Academy, no. 241, 1832.',NULL,'2009-06-25 15:11:07'),(72,'MAG0072',22,'\'The identical Peter . . . an immense cocked hat.\' [4 lines]','--- - \"187\" - \"188\" - \"18\" - \"251\" - \"319\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\"',56,57,3,'8 x 7','1832','1832',31,'vol. 36 (title-page vignette)','EUL, Corson A.7.a.1829-33/36','','Depicts Peter Peebles in Parliament Close, home of the Court of Session in Edinburgh, with the equestrian statue of Charles II prominent i