diers, his mother Elspat having fainted on the floor of the hut. [Ch. 11; EEWN 20, 110]',NULL,NULL),(82,'MAG0082',13,'\'I must obey you mother . . . instantly was fast asleep.\' [4 lines]','--- - \"207\" - \"208\" - \"327\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\"',41,114,3,'7.5 x 7','1832','1832',31,'vol. 41 (title-page vignette)','EUL, Corson A.7.a.1829-33/41','','Depicts Hamish MacTavish succumbing to the effect of the sleeping potion administered by his mother, who looks over him. [Ch. 11; EEWN 20, 97.5-8]',NULL,NULL),(83,'MAG0083',9,'Fair Maid of Perth.','--- - \"209\" - \"210\" - \"211\" - \"98\" - \"103\" - \"155\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\"',2,39,3,'7.5 x 11','1832','1832',31,'vol. 42 (frontispiece)','EUL, Corson A.7.a.1829-33/42','','Depicts Catharine Glover leaning over and kissing Henry Gow, asleep in a chair, with her father Simon appearing at the door [Ch. 5; EEWN 21, 49-50]',NULL,NULL),(84,'MAG0084',9,'\'He beheld stretched beneath him . . . and its towers.\' [3 lines]','--- \n- \"49\"\n- \"116\"\n- \"213\"\n- \"212\"\n',52,69,3,'9 x 7','1832','1832',31,'vol. 42 (title-page vignette)','EUL, Corson A.7.a.1829-33/42','','Depicts the traveller on horseback surveying the valley of the Tay with the town of Perth in the distance [Ch. 1; EEWN 21, 27-30]. Also found as a vignette in \'Tales and Romances of the Author of Waverley\' 16mo and 18mo sets, though the engraver differs. ',NULL,'2009-06-25 15:18:59'),(85,'MAG0085',9,'Fair Maid of Perth / \'At the foot of a rock . . . of a Carthusian monk.\' [4 lines]','--- \n- \"214\"\n- \"210\"\n- \"288\"\n- \"72\"\n- \"88\"\n',31,57,3,'10.5 x 8','1832','1832',31,'vol. 43 (frontispiece)','EUL, Corson A.7.a.1829-33/43','','Depicts Catharine Glover listening devoutly to instructions from Father Clement, under a rock beneath the hill of Kinnoul [Ch. 14; EEWN 21, 145.30-33].',NULL,'2009-06-25 15:19:26'),(86,'MAG0086',9,'\'\"A lute . . . from whence the music comes.\"\' [3 lines]','--- \n- \"8\"\n- \"524\"\n- \"74\"\n- \"244\"\n- \"215\"\n- \"212\"\n',52,69,3,'6.5 x 8.5','1832','1832',31,'vol. 43 (title-page vignette)','EUL, Corson A.7.a.1829-33/43','','Depicts the barge of the Duke of Rothesay on the River Tay, as Rothesay hears the music of Louise the French glee-maiden from Henshaw\'s boat [Ch. 30; EEWN 21, 323.6-8]. Also features as vignette in 1833 \'Tales and Romances\' 16mo set, vol 12 (see #NTD0045), though the engraver differs. ',NULL,'2009-08-14 07:50:17'),(87,'MAG0087',2,'Anne of Geierstein. / \'As Margaret spoke . . . back against his breast.\' [7 lines]','--- - \"216\" - \"217\" - \"218\" - \"219\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\"',69,44,3,'9.5 x 8','1833','1833',31,'vol. 44 (frontispiece)','EUL, Corson A.7.a.1829-33/44','','Depicts Margaret of Anjou on the ramparts of the monastery at Mont Sainte Victoire, having thrown her sable feather and red rose into the wind, with Arthur Philipson looking on. [Ch. 30; EEWN 22, 339.36-42]',NULL,NULL),(88,'MAG0088',2,'\'Ha! Scharfgerichter . . . preparing for thy duty?\' [2 lines]','--- - \"220\" - \"221\" - \"103\" - \"222\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\"',9,58,3,'9 x 7','1833','1833',31,'vol. 44 (title-page vignette)','EUL, Corson A.7.a.1829-33/44','','Depicts Archibald von Hagenbach in his torture-chamber surveying Francis Steinernherz preparing a two-handed sword in readiness for execution. [Ch. 14; EEWN 22, 143.12-13]',NULL,NULL),(89,'MAG0089',2,'Anne of Geirstein [sic] / \'\"Young man,\" . . . with dreadful gusts of wind.\' [6 lines]','--- \n- \"216\"\n- \"219\"\n- \"217\"\n',105,88,3,'10.5 x 7.5','1833','1833',31,'vol. 45 (frontispiece)','EUL, Corson A.7.a.1829-33/45','','Depicts Margaret of Anjou seated at the monastery at Mont Sainte Victoire with Arthur Philipson in attendance behind her [Ch. 30; EEWN 22, 336.43-337.1-4].',NULL,'2009-04-10 12:12:05'),(90,'MAG0090',2,'\'Annette sped up a narrow turnpike stair . . . they are come!\' [4 lines]','--- - \"223\" - \"224\" - \"225\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\"',111,90,3,'8.5 x 6.5','1833','1833',31,'vol. 45 (title-page vignette)','EUL, Corson A.7.a.1829-33/45','','Depicts Annette Veilchen rushing into Anne of Geierstein\'s apartment at Arnheim Castle to announce the arrival of Arthur Philipson. [Ch. 21; EEWN 22, 236.17-20]',NULL,NULL),(91,'MAG0091',8,'Count Robert of Paris / \'Without a moment\'s hesitation . . . caress a large wolf-hound.\' [5 lines)','--- \n- \"103\"\n- \"18\"\n- \"26\"\n- \"49\"\n- \"226\"\n',12,45,3,'9.5 x 7.5','1833','1833',31,'vol. 46 (frontispiece)','EUL, Corson A.7.a.1829-33/46','0030050d.jpg#http://images.is.ed.ac.uk/luna/servlet/detail/UoEwal~1~1~58476~100378','Depicts Count Robert of Paris seated on the Emperor\'s throne, with wolf-hound at his side [Ch. 9; EEWN 23a, 106.35-37]. See image (from 1879 reprint).',NULL,'2009-06-25 15:25:27'),(92,'MAG0092',8,'\'The assassin hovered . . . it was designed to protect.\' [3 lines]','--- - \"227\" - \"228\" - \"229\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\"',105,43,3,'6.5 x 8','1833','1833',31,'vol. 46 (title-page vignette)','EUL, Corson A.7.a.1829-33/46','','Depicts Sebastes of Mitylene moving towards the sleeping figure of Hereward in an attempt to assassinate him. [Ch. 2; EEWN 23a, 21.25-27]',NULL,NULL),(93,'MAG0093',7,'Castle Dangerous.','--- - \"237\" - \"310\" - \"238\" - \"96\" - \"38\" - \"26\" - \"103\" - \"320\" - \"109\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\" - \"\"',94,95,3,'8 x 10','1833','1833',31,'vol. 47 (frontispiece)','EUL, Corson A.7.a.1829-33/47','','Depicts Sir Aymer de Valence, guided by old woman into the vaulted apartment of the sexton at Douglas Kirk, Lazarus Powheid, with the page Fabian looking on from the doorway. [Ch. 15; EEWN 23b, 91-92]',NULL,NULL),(94,'MAG0094',7,'\'The trooper, wrapping part of a mantle round her head, lent his arm to support her in this blinded state.\'','--- 