 image), and with artist given as Peter De Wint and engraver as Charles Heath.',NULL,'2009-06-25 15:26:07'),(98,'NTD0002',28,'[Holyrood Palace]','--- \n- \"251\"\n- \"48\"\n- \"311\"\n- \"72\"\n',71,67,1,'5.5 x 8','1821','1821',14,'vol. 2 (title-page vignette)','EUL, Corson A.7.a.1821/2','0014638d.jpg#http://images.is.ed.ac.uk/luna/servlet/detail/UoEwal~1~1~57172~100299','Depicts Holyrood Palace, the Salisbury Crags, and Arthur\'s Seat, Edinburgh. Illustration caption as given in \'Sixteen Engravings from Real Scenes Supposed to be Described in the Novels and Tales of the Author of Waverley\' (Edinburgh: Constable & Co., 1821). Vignette also on title-page of \'Novels and Tales of the Author of Waverley\' (2nd 8vo issue), 12 vols (Edinburgh: Constable & Co., 1822), vol. 2; and in \'The Waverley Album\' (London: Charles Heath, [1832]), facing p. 4, titled there \'Holyrood Palace\' (see image) and with artist given as Peter De Wint and engraver as Charles Heath.',NULL,'2009-04-10 12:20:30'),(99,'NTD0003',11,'[Caerlaveroc Castle]','--- \n- \"14\"\n- \"108\"\n- \"245\"\n',71,67,1,'6 x 8','1821','1821',14,'vol. 3 (title-page vignette)','EUL, Corson A.7.a.1821/3','0007423d.jpg#http://images.is.ed.ac.uk/luna/servlet/detail/UoEwal~1~1~53711~100093','Depicts Caerlaverock Castle (ruins), as an equivalent of the old castle of Ellangowan. Illustration caption as given in \'Sixteen Engravings from Real Scenes Supposed to be Described in the Novels and Tales of the Author of Waverley\' (Edinburgh: Constable & Co., 1821). Vignette also on title-page of \'Novels and Tales of the Author of Waverley\' (2nd 8vo issue), 12 vols (Edinburgh: Constable & Co., 1822), vol. 3; and in \'The Waverley Album\' (London: Charles Heath, [1832]), facing p. 5, titled there \'Ellangowan Castle\' (see image); and with artist given as Peter De Wint and engraver as Charles Heath.',NULL,'2009-06-25 15:26:34'),(100,'NTD0004',11,'[Dunure Castle]','--- \n- \"8\"\n- \"14\"\n- \"108\"\n- \"245\"\n- \"140\"\n',7