acing p. 126','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts a Highland banquet attended by Waverley and Fergus MacIvor among many others, with Mac-Murrough, the family bard, to the left of the picture, with arm in air, as guests listen and drink, one raising his own arm in exultation [Ch. 20]. ','2009-05-10 12:48:31','2009-06-26 12:49:54'),(946,'DRY0006',28,'Flora and Waverley at the Waterfall','--- \n- \"36\"\n- \"242\"\n- \"41\"\n- \"60\"\n- \"74\"\n- \"351\"\n- \"102\"\n',168,165,6,'14 x 9.5','1892','1892',45,'vol. 1, facing p. 138','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Flora playing a harp, in the Glen at Glennaquoich with the waterfall behind her, and Waverley appearing from below [Ch. 22].','2009-05-10 12:54:09','2009-05-10 12:54:09'),(947,'DRY0007',28,'Mrs. Mucklewrath Defies her Spouse','--- \n- \"103\"\n- \"353\"\n- \"17\"\n- \"436\"\n- \"437\"\n',168,165,6,'9.5 x 14','1892','1892',45,'vol. 1, facing p. 196','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts John Mucklewrath the blacksmith in his smithy, with a long rod menacingly in his hand, being berated by his wife, who has a small child in one arm, while bystanders look on, and one figure (apparently a clergyman) attempts to intervene; another workman, to the left, stands erect in front of a pile of swords and guns [Ch. 30].','2009-05-10 12:56:39','2009-06-26 12:51:03'),(948,'DRY0008',28,'The Ball at Holyrood','--- \n- \"12\"\n- \"155\"\n- \"53\"\n- \"262\"\n- \"60\"\n- \"301\"\n- \"102\"\n',168,165,6,'9.5 x 14','1892','1892',45,'vol. 1, facing p. 272','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Waverley at the Holyrood Ball bowing before the seated figures of Rose and Flora, while a kilted Fergus looks on, and with Charles Edward observing from another group [Ch. 43].','2009-05-10 12:59:59','2009-05-10 12:59:59'),(949,'DRY0009',28,'‘Forward! Sons of Ivor!’','--- \n- \"103\"\n- \"46\"\n- \"262\"\n',168,165,6,'9.5 x 14','1892','1892',45,'vol. 1, facing p. 296','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Fergus, sword pointing forward and shield on other arms, exhorting his heavily armed clansmen to charge at Prestonpans [Ch. 47].','2009-05-10 13:05:11','2009-05-10 13:05:11'),(950,'DRY0010',28,'Waverley\'s Adieu to Flora','--- \n- \"172\"\n- \"53\"\n- \"60\"\n- \"102\"\n',168,165,6,'14 x 9.5','1892','1892',45,'vol. 1, facing p. 426','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Waverley bowing and kissing the hand of the Flora, who is standing and turns her face away, with a nun-like figure behind her; a painting of Prince Charles Edward in armour hangs on the wall [Ch. 68].','2009-05-10 13:08:07','2009-05-10 13:08:07'),(951,'DRY0011',11,'Meg Merrilies in Dirk Hatteraick\'s Cave','--- \n- \"103\"\n- \"266\"\n- \"314\"\n- \"24\"\n- \"252\"\n- \"42\"\n- \"265\"\n- \"142\"\n',169,165,6,'14.7 x 9.5','1892','1892',45,'vol. 2 (frontispiece)','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts the Meg Merrilies standing accusingly with one armed raised before the seated figure of Dirk Hatteraick in his cave, an empty bottle at his feet, with the faces of (apparently) Bertram and Dinmont faintly visible behind him [Ch. 54].','2009-05-10 13:11:06','2009-06-26 12:51:50'),(952,'DRY0012',11,'Dominie Sampson in the Library','--- \n- \"163\"\n- \"57\"\n- \"92\"\n',169,165,6,'7.3 x 5','1892','1892',45,'vol. 2 (title-page vignette)','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Dominie Sampson both arms raised staring in rapture at a pile of books in the library at Woodbourne [Ch. 20]. Title/caption from List of Illustrations.','2009-05-10 13:15:50','2009-06-26 12:52:24'),(953,'DRY0013',11,'Mannering Benighted','--- \n- \"49\"\n- \"52\"\n- \"63\"\n- \"129\"\n',169,165,6,'15 x 9','1892','1892',45,'vol. 2, facing p. 4','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Guy Mannering on horseback being guided by Jock Jabos at nightfall through a gap in a stone wall [Ch. 1].','2009-05-10 13:18:09','2009-05-10 13:18:09'),(954,'DRY0014',11,'Meg Merrilies’ Malediction on the Laird','--- \n- \"225\"\n- \"263\"\n- \"252\"\n- \"49\"\n- \"188\"\n- \"265\"\n',169,165,6,'15 x 9','1892','1892',45,'vol. 2, facing p. 50','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts 