Ch. 28].','2009-06-15 08:29:01','2009-06-15 08:29:01'),(1313,'BOR0231',2,'The Funeral of the Queen','--- \n- \"109\"\n- \"216\"\n- \"88\"\n',214,192,2,'13.7 x 9.1','1894','1894',44,'vol. 44, facing p. 288','NLS, Lit.S.22','','Depicts the funeral of Margaret of Anjou, as the coffin is carried by its bearers, in the cathedral at Aix [Ch. 33].','2009-06-15 08:30:22','2009-06-15 08:30:22'),(1314,'BOR0232',8,'Hereward Rescues Bertha','--- \n- \"103\"\n- \"407\"\n- \"228\"\n- \"409\"\n',215,181,2,'13.7 x 9.2','1894','1894',44,'vol. 45 (frontispiece)','NLS, Lit.S.22','','Depicts Hereward in a wooded area with axe uplifted protecting Bertha from Sylvanus, who withdraws in a crouching fashion [Ch. 20].','2009-06-15 08:32:02','2009-06-15 08:33:33'),(1315,'BOR0233',8,'Hereward Before Alexis','--- \n- \"533\"\n- \"535\"\n- \"163\"\n- \"228\"\n- \"534\"\n',215,147,2,'9.2 x 14.3','1894','1894',44,'vol. 45, facing p. 64','NLS, Lit.S.22','','Depicts Hereward saluting the Imperial court, with Alexius, Irene, and their daughter Anna Comnena all seated on thrones, and two female slaves seated at a table below, attending to a number of scrolls [Ch. 3].','2009-06-15 08:37:04','2009-06-15 08:37:04'),(1316,'BOR0234',8,'Agelastes and Hereward','--- \n- \"408\"\n- \"34\"\n- \"228\"\n',215,190,2,'13.8 x 9.2','1894','1894',44,'vol. 45, facing p. 160','NLS, Lit.S.22','','Depicts Hereward entering through a path through woods and confronting Agelastes, who is seated among the ruins [Ch. 7].\r\n\r\n','2009-06-15 08:50:35','2009-06-15 08:50:35'),(1317,'BOR0235',8,'Count Robert Meets Agelastes','--- \n- \"408\"\n- \"163\"\n- \"410\"\n- \"226\"\n',215,179,2,'14 x 9.5','1894','1894',44,'vol. 45, facing p. 224','NLS, Lit.S.22','','Depicts the Countess Brenhilda and Count Robert by an archway encountering the seated Agelastes, who holds a roll of parchment in his lap [Ch. 10].','2009-06-15 08:52:01','2009-06-15 08:52:01'),(1318,'BOR0236',8,'In the Dungeon','--- \n- \"226\"\n- \"85\"\n',215,191,2,'14 x 9.2','1894','1894',44,'vol. 45, facing p. 288','NLS, Lit.S.22','','Depicts Count Robert by his bed in prison with an uplifted stool, warding off the tiger that lurks at the far end of the room [Ch. 15].','2009-06-15 08:53:26','2009-06-28 14:34:54'),(1319,'BOR0237',8,'The Combat','--- \n- \"103\"\n- \"296\"\n- \"228\"\n- \"226\"\n',215,176,2,'13.8 x 9.2','1894','1894',44,'vol. 46 (frontispiece)','NLS, Lit.S.22','','Depicts Count Robert in the lists with axe raised ready to strike towards the uplifted shield of Hereward, who falls backwards, both combatants fighting on foot [Ch. 34]. ','2009-06-15 08:54:50','2009-06-15 08:54:50'),(1320,'BOR0238',8,'Bertha in the Camp','--- \n- \"407\"\n- \"49\"\n- \"320\"\n',215,157,2,'13.7 x 9.2','1894','1894',44,'vol. 46, facing p. 54','NLS, Lit.S.22','','Depicts Bertha with an accompanying soldier arriving at the camp of the Crusaders, with the a number of mounted young knights facing her with jocular expressions [Ch. 23].','2009-06-15 08:56:13','2009-06-15 08:56:13'),(1321,'BOR0239',8,'Ursel on the Terrace','--- \n- \"537\"\n- \"327\"\n- \"85\"\n- \"536\"\n',215,191,2,'13.8 x 9.2','1894','1894',44,'vol. 46, facing p. 134','NLS, Lit.S.22','','Depicts the released (and supposedly blind) Ursel on a terrace cowering from the sunlight, and attended by a robed figure presumably meant to represent the physician Douban (though Alexius Comnenus himself is another possibility) [Ch. 29].','2009-06-15 08:59:01','2009-06-28 14:35:19'),(1322,'BOR0240',25,'In the Hospital','--- \n- \"336\"\n- \"538\"\n- \"178\"\n',216,191,2,'13.8 x 9.2','1894','1894',44,'vol. 46, facing p. 358','NLS, Lit.S.22','','Depicts Richard Middlemas lying in the hospital of the East India Company on the Isle of Wight, as Seelencooper as its Governor stands above him with two attendants [Ch. 20].','2009-06-15 09:02:26','2009-06-19 10:39:19'),(1323,'BOR0241',25,'The Pretended Fakir','--- \n- \"540\"\n- \"247\"\n- \"539\"\n',216,152,2,'13.7 x 9.4','1894','1894',44,'vol. 46, facing p. 470','NLS, Lit.S.22','','Depicts Hyder Ali flinging away the cap and fake beard which had disguised him as the Fakir, in front of his surprised son Tippoo; elephants and their riders can be seen in the background [Ch. 28].','2009-06-15 09:05:36','2009-06-19 10:41:07'),(1324,'BOR0242',7,'Douglas Castle','--- \n- \"14\"\n',157,146,2,'14 x 9.3','1894','1894',44,'vol. 47 (frontispiece)','NLS, Lit.S.22','','Depicts Castle Douglas elevated above a sheet of water [Ch. 5].','2009-06-15 09:07:30','2009-06-15 09:07:30'),(1325,'BOR0243',7,'The Travellers','--- \n- \"231\"\n- \"541\"\n- \"116\"\n',157,146,2,'14 x 9.4','1894','1894',44,'vol. 47, facing p. 6','NLS, Lit.S.22','','Depicts Bertram the minstrel accompanying Lady Augusta (in disguise) over open countryside [Ch. 2].','2009-06-15 09:09:55','2009-06-28 14:36:04'),(1326,'BOR0244',7,'The Hunting Feast','--- \n- \"103\"\n- \"26\"\n- \"50\"\n- \"230\"\n',157,146,2,'14 x 9.3','1894','1894',44,'vol. 47, facing p. 96','NLS, Lit.S.22','','Depicts Michael Turnbull standing by a table at the hunting feast, with a long partisan (spear) in one hand and a tankard in the other [Ch. 7].','2009-06-15 09:11:45','2009-06-28 14:36:22'),(1327,'BOR0245',7,'The Escape','--- \n- \"231\"\n- \"38\"\n- \"542\"\n- \"219\"\n- \"288\"\n',157,146,2,'9 x 14.5','1894','1894',44,'vol. 47, facing p. 192','NLS, Lit.S.22','','Depicts Lady Augusta and Sister Ursula outside a doorway in St Bride’s Convent, from which they are escaping [Ch. 11].','2009-06-15 09:15:25','2009-06-28 14:36:43'),(1328,'BOR0246',7,'The Lady Watches the Combat','--- \n- \"231\"\n- \"296\"\n- \"544\"\n- \"320\"\n- \"543\"\n',157,146,2,'13.7 x 9.2','1894','1894',44,'vol. 47, facing p. 246','NLS, Lit.S.22','','Depicts Lady Augusta at some distance watching the combat, on foot and with swords, between Sir John de Walton and Sir James Douglas in a dingle called the Bloody Sykes [Ch. 17].','2009-06-15 09:18:34','2009-06-15 09:18:34'),(1329,'BOR0247',27,'On the Road','--- \n- \"15\"\n- \"116\"\n- \"333\"\n- \"117\"\n',217,143,2,'13.8 x 9.3','1894','1894',44,'vol. 48 (frontispiece)','NLS, Lit.S.22','','Depicts a herd of Highland cattle along a drove road, with the front animals drinking in water, and with an indistinct figure of a drover, representing Robin ‘Oig’ McCombich, behind them [Ch. 13].','2009-06-15 09:26:39','2009-06-15 09:26:39'),(1330,'BOR0248',13,'At Elspat\'s Hut','--- \n- \"225\"\n- \"545\"\n- \"49\"\n- \"116\"\n- \"546\"\n',217,143,2,'14.1 x 9.6','1894','1894',44,'vol. 48, facing p. 112','NLS, Lit.S.22','','Depicts the carriage of Mrs Bethune Baliol and her travelling companion with the postilion Donald MacLeish on the lead horse, near the site of Elspat MacTavish’s hut [Ch. 7] \r\n\r\n','2009-06-15 09:32:01','2009-06-15 09:32:01'),(1331,'BOR0249',13,'Execution of Hamish','--- \n- \"46\"\n- \"207\"\n- \"222\"\n- \"96\"\n',217,143,2,'13.9 x 9.4','1894','1894',44,'vol. 48, facing p. 182','NLS, Lit.S.22','','Depicts Hamish MacTavish bound and kneeling on his coffin facing an execution squad [Ch. 11].','2009-06-15 09:34:23','2009-06-15 09:34:23'),(1332,'BOR0250',31,'Before the Mirror','--- \n- \"326\"\n- \"468\"\n- \"471\"\n- \"469\"\n',217,143,2,'9.4 x 14.5','1894','1894',44,'vol. 48, facing p. 288','NLS, Lit.S.22','','Depicts Lady Bothwell and Lady Forester, alongside Doctor Damiotti, looking towards the mirror, with a skull, crossed swords, and burning tapers among surrounding objects [Ch. 2].','2009-06-15 09:36:09','2009-06-15 09:36:09'),(1333,'BOR0251',32,'The Tapestried Chamber','--- \n- \"284\"\n- \"473\"\n',217,143,2,'14 x 9.5','1894','1894',44,'vol. 48, facing p. 310','NLS, Lit.S.22','','Depicts General Browne starting up out of his bed while a guest at Woodville Castle and looking at the apparition of a female ghost standing between the bed and the fireplace.','2009-06-15 09:37:46','2009-06-15 09:37:46'),(1334,'DRY0081',14,'Rebecca Defying the Templar','--- \n- \"9\"\n- \"14\"\n- \"105\"\n',169,165,6,'14 x 9.5','1893',