ailie','--- \n- \"103\"\n- \"120\"\n- \"67\"\n- \"288\"\n',172,165,6,'9.5 x 14.5','1893','1893',45,'vol. 10, facing p. 82','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Christie of Clinthill, sword by side, dismissively fingering the collar of the Baillie, who holds a lantern in one hand, in the refectory of the Monastery of Saint Mary’s, as several of the monks look on [Ch. 10]','2009-06-16 12:10:07','2009-06-16 12:10:07'),(1349,'DRY0096',17,'Mary Avenel at her Lessons','--- \n- \"112\"\n- \"163\"\n- \"289\"\n- \"121\"\n',172,165,6,'14.4 x 9.5','1893','1893',45,'vol. 10, facing p. 92','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Mary Avenel seated at her studies with Edward Glendinning, with Halbert standing in the doorway appealing to them to leave these [Ch. 11].','2009-06-16 12:11:57','2009-06-16 12:11:57'),(1350,'DRY0097',17,'Sir Piercie Shafton at Glendearg','--- \n- \"120\"\n- \"18\"\n- \"67\"\n- \"287\"\n- \"290\"\n',172,165,6,'9.3 x 14.4','1893','1893',45,'vol. 10, facing p. 122','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts the extravagantly-attired Sir Piercie sitting at table in Glendearg face tilted towards the ceiling, with Christie of Clinthill seated opposite and Elspeth Glendinning attending to them; the younger members of the family group are positioned in the recess of a window [Ch. 14].','2009-06-16 12:13:53','2009-06-28 14:38:52'),(1351,'DRY0098',17,'Mary Interceding with Halbert','--- \n- \"103\"\n- \"112\"\n- \"382\"\n- \"121\"\n',172,165,6,'14. 6 x 9.5','1893','1893',45,'vol. 10, facing p. 190','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Mary Avenel in a shawl outside Glendearg at dawn appealing to Halbert Glendinning (who holds a crossbow and wears a sword) to refrain from violence [Ch. 21].','2009-06-16 12:19:25','2009-06-16 12:19:25'),(1352,'DRY0099',17,'Julian Avenel Caressing the Goshawk','--- \n- \"342\"\n- \"191\"\n- \"343\"\n- \"50\"\n',172,165,6,'14. 6 x 9.5','1893','1893',45,'vol. 10, facing p. 220','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Julian Avenel, a large sword by his side, looking quizzically at a falcon which he holds on one hand, while Catherine sits uneasily and apparently ignored in the fireplace of his Hall [Ch. 24].\r\n\r\n','2009-06-16 12:21:52','2009-06-16 12:21:52'),(1353,'DRY0100',17,'Escape of Sir Piercie Shafton from Glendearg','--- \n- \"382\"\n- \"318\"\n- \"49\"\n- \"290\"\n',172,165,6,'14.4 x 9.3','1893','1893',45,'vol. 10, facing p. 270','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Sir Piercie Shafton on horseback, with Mysie Happer seated behind him, galloping away from the Tower of Glendearg [Ch. 28].','2009-06-16 16:50:19','2009-06-16 16:50:19'),(1354,'DRY0101',1,'Roland Graeme and Adam Woodcock','--- \n- \"191\"\n- \"296\"\n- \"123\"\n- \"50\"\n- \"550\"\n',172,165,6,'14.3 x 9.3','1893','1893',45,'vol. 11 (frontispiece)','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Roland Graeme assaulting Adam Woodcock, the falconer at Avenel, whose raised hand is gloved; perched falcons and Woodcock’s assistant can be seen behind [Ch. 4].','2009-06-16 16:52:46','2009-06-16 16:52:46'),(1355,'DRY0102',1,'Adam Woodcock, Falconer','--- \n- \"191\"\n- \"50\"\n- \"550\"\n',172,165,6,'8 x 5','1893','1893',45,'vol. 11 (title-page vignette)','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Adam Woodcock, with a falcon on hand and looking skywards, in open countryside. Apparently not incident specific. Title/caption from List of Illustrations.','2009-06-16 16:55:24','2009-06-16 16:55:24'),(1356,'DRY0103',1,'Roland Graeme and the Lady of Avenel','--- \n- \"112\"\n- \"324\"\n- \"17\"\n- \"123\"\n',172,165,6,'9.4 x 14.5','1893','1893',45,'vol. 11, facing p. 20','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Roland Graeme as a boy on the ramparts of Avenel Castle parading with a stick, while the Lady of Avenel looks on, with Lilias behind her [Ch. 3].\r\n\r\n','2009-06-16 16:58:22','2009-06-16 16:58:22'),(1357,'DRY0104',1,'Roland and Magdalen Graeme in the Cell of St. Cuthbert','--- \n- \"109\"\n- \"414\"\n- \"123\"\n- \"245\"\n',172,165,6,'14.3 x 9.1','1893','1893',45,'vol. 11, facing p. 70','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Roland Graeme standing at a window in the ruined Cell and looking towards Magdalen Graeme, who stands upright in a cloak-like habit with hands clasped [Ch. 8].','2009-06-16 17:01:16','2009-06-16 17:02:06'),(1358,'DRY0105',1,'Father Ambrose and the Abbot of Unreason','--- \n- \"395\"\n- \"33\"\n- \"289\"\n- \"288\"\n',172,165,6,'14.3 x 9.3','1893','1893',45,'vol. 11, facing p. 122','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Father Ambrose (Edward Glendinning) in his full vestments facing the intruding Abbot of Unreason, with  Roland Graeme to the side looking on [Ch. 14].','2009-06-16 17:04:20','2009-06-16 17:04:20'),(1359,'DRY0106',1,'The Regent Murray Dismissing the Council','--- \n- \"225\"\n- \"48\"\n- \"383\"\n',172,165,6,'14.5 x 9.4','1893','1893',45,'vol. 11, facing p. 176','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts the Earl of Murray at Holyrood Palace having dismissed his council after a meeting, with two of the privy-councillors lingering in the doorway [Ch. 18].','2009-06-16 17:06:47','2009-06-16 17:06:47'),(1360,'DRY0107',1,'Queen Mary in the Garden at Lochleven Castle','--- \n- \"225\"\n- \"34\"\n- \"128\"\n- \"122\"\n',172,165,6,'14.4 x 9.3','1893','1893',45,'vol. 11, facing p. 218','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Queen Mary in the closed garden at Loch Leven Castle with two female attendants [Ch. 21].','2009-06-16 17:08:32','2009-06-16 17:08:32'),(1361,'DRY0108',1,'Catherine Seyton and Roland Graeme','--- \n- \"225\"\n- \"18\"\n- \"155\"\n- \"123\"\n- \"325\"\n',172,165,6,'14.8 x 9.2','1893','1893',45,'vol. 11, facing p. 264','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Roland Graeme kneeling before and holding the hand of Catherine Seyton, who is seated and wears an ornamented dress [Ch. 24].\r\n\r\n','2009-06-16 17:10:46','2009-06-28 14:39:32'),(1362,'DRY0109',1,'Discovery of the Attempted Flight by the Lady of Lochleven','--- \n- \"103\"\n- \"225\"\n- \"489\"\n- \"490\"\n- \"122\"\n',172,165,6,'9.4 x 14.5','1893','1893',45,'vol. 11, facing p. 322','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts the Lady of Lochleven pointing accusingly at Mary Queen of Scots, who is seated at the other end of a large fireplace, with (apparently) George Douglas also there standing defiantly with hand on the hilt of his sword [Ch. 30].','2009-06-16 17:13:45','2009-06-28 14:40:25'),(1363,'DRY0110',1,'Queen Mary\'s Departure from Scotland','--- \n- \"225\"\n- \"8\"\n- \"123\"\n- \"122\"\n',172,165,6,'14.7 x 9.5','1893','1893',45,'vol. 11, facing p. 424','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Roland Graeme kneeling and kissing the hand of Mary Queen of Scots, as she stands with her attendant at the water’s edge about to embark from Scotland; the sail of a boat is faintly visible behind [Ch. 38].','2009-06-16 17:15:40','2009-06-16 17:15:40'),(1364,'DRY0111',15,'Amy Examining the Earl\'s Jewels','--- \n- \"130\"\n- \"131\"\n- \"56\"\n- \"89\"\n',218,165,6,'14.5 x 9.5','1893','1893',45,'vol. 12 (frontispiece)','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Amy Robsart at Cumnor Place, beneath the seated Earl of Leicester, examining a chivalric collar worn by the Earl [Ch. 7].','2009-06-16 17:17:42','2009-06-16 17:19:47'),(1365,'DRY0112',15,'The Death of Amy','--- \n- \"229\"\n- \"89\"\n',218,165,6,'6.5 x 8','1893','1893',45,'vol. 12 (title-page vignette)','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts the body of Amy Robsart face up, and with arms outstretched, at the foot of a flight of steps [Ch. 41]. Title/caption from List of Illustrations.','2009-06-16 17:21:04','2009-06-16 17:21:04'),(1366,'DRY0113',15,'Tressilian and Wayland Smith','--- \n- \"353\"\n- \"314\"\n- \"346\"\n- \"95\"\n- \"345\"\n',218,165,6,'14.4 x 9.4','1893','1893',45,'vol. 12, facing p. 114','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Tressilian confronting Wayland Smith outside the entrance to his forge, the latter attired in a bear-skin hat and holding up a hammer, with Sludge (‘Flibbertigibbet’) mischievously looking on [Ch. 10].','2009-06-16 17:23:09','2009-06-16 17:23:09'),(1367,'DRY0114',15,'The Earl of Sussex takes Wayland\'s Potion','--- \n- \"327\"\n- \"178\"\n- \"95\"\n- \"551\"\n- \"345\"\n'