ey Peveril mounted on Black Hastings grappling with and impeding the path of Major Bridgenorth, with various armed men also on horses watching [Ch. 7].\r\n\r\n','2009-06-17 13:28:36','2009-06-28 14:45:53'),(1397,'DRY0144',19,'Lady Peveril Surprised Near the Dobby\'s Walk','--- \n- \"49\"\n- \"129\"\n- \"503\"\n',221,165,6,'13. 5 x 9.4','1894','1894',45,'vol. 15, facing p. 112','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Lady Peveril under a tree beside a pathway, in moonlight, with the first of a body of riders (presumably meant to represent the party of Sir Geoffrey) drawing up in front of her [Ch. 10].','2009-06-17 13:30:31','2009-06-17 13:30:31'),(1398,'DRY0145',19,'Julian and Fenella on the Castle Rock','--- \n- \"157\"\n- \"143\"\n- \"153\"\n',221,165,6,'14.2 x 9.4','1894','1894',45,'vol. 15, facing p. 178','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Julian Peveril on the steps outside Holm-Peel Castle, and Fenella above him with arms outstretched [Ch. 16].','2009-06-17 13:32:06','2009-06-28 14:46:37'),(1399,'DRY0146',19,'Julian Attempts to Rescue his Father','--- \n- \"103\"\n- \"154\"\n- \"296\"\n- \"153\"\n- \"503\"\n- \"297\"\n- \"85\"\n- \"96\"\n',221,165,6,'9.5 x 14.2','1894','1894',45,'vol. 15, facing p. 268','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Julian Peveril at Peveril Castle attacking with his sword the soldiers guarding his father, whose hands are tied behind his back, and as Lady Peveril looks on anxiously; the figure at a writing-table on the other side of the room is presumably meant to represent Major Bridgenorth [Ch. 23].','2009-06-17 13:34:41','2009-06-28 14:47:10'),(1400,'DRY0147',19,'The Attack on Moultrassie Hall','--- \n- \"353\"\n- \"152\"\n- \"154\"\n- \"153\"\n',221,165,6,'14.8 x 9.2','1894','1894',45,'vol. 15, facing p. 300','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts the attack on Moultrassie Hall, from which smoke billows, and where Alice Bridgenorth appears on a staircase, with Julian (apparently) descending the stairs towards the main groupings of  assailants and defenders, among whom