e event [Ch. 37].','2009-06-17 20:01:28','2009-06-17 20:01:28'),(1414,'DRY0161',24,'Meg Dods\'s Alarm at Tyrrel\'s Return','--- \n- \"402\"\n- \"240\"\n- \"401\"\n',222,165,6,'14.5 x 9.5','1894','1894',45,'vol. 17 (frontispiece)','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Frank Tyrrel, in cloak and hat and holding a horse whip, entering through the doorway of the kitchen at the Cleikum Inn, with Meg Dods holding out her hands in a gesture of alarm and disbelief [Ch. 28].','2009-06-17 20:03:08','2009-06-17 20:04:15'),(1415,'DRY0162',24,'Clara Before the Mirror','--- \n- \"18\"\n- \"177\"\n',222,165,6,'8 x 5','1894','1894',45,'vol. 17 (title-page vignette)','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Clara Mowbray standing before a wall mirror and untying her hair hair, following the instructions of her brother to prepare herself for Lord Etherington [Ch. 23]. Title/caption from List of Illustrations.','2009-06-17 20:05:31','2009-06-17 20:05:31'),(1416,'DRY0163',24,'Meg Dods\'s Reception of Tyrrel','--- \n- \"402\"\n- \"240\"\n- \"401\"\n- \"98\"\n',222,165,6,'14.7 x 9.5','1894','1894',45,'vol. 17, facing p. 14','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Meg Dods in her kitchen polishing a candlestick while warily receiving Frank Tyrrel, who wears a riding cloak and hat and holds a whip by his side [Ch. 2].','2009-06-17 20:07:23','2009-06-17 20:07:23'),(1417,'DRY0164',24,'Lady Penelope\'s Tea-Party','--- \n- \"510\"\n',222,165,6,'14.7 x 9.5','1894','1894',45,'vol. 17, facing p. 66','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Lady Penelope Penfeather seated at a tea-table, with two footmen standing behind her, and a waiting woman attending to a tray on the table [Ch. 7].','2009-06-17 20:08:46','2009-06-17 20:08:46'),(1418,'DRY0165',24,'Tyrrel Puts Aside Sir Bingo Binks','--- \n- \"481\"\n- \"401\"\n',222,165,6,'14.7 x 9.5','1894','1894',45,'vol. 17, facing p. 88','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Frank Tyrrel, cane in hand, brushing aside Sir Bingo Binks from the doorway, as he leaves the Fox Hotel [Ch. 8].','2009-06-17 20:09:57','2009-06-17 20:09:57'),(1419,'DRY0166',24,'Meg Dods Confronting Captain MacTurk','--- \n- \"296\"\n- \"402\"\n- \"240\"\n- \"403\"\n',222,165,6,'14.5 x 9.2','1894','1894',45,'vol. 17, facing p. 126','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Meg Dods assaulting Captain MacTurk with a broom outside the Cleikum Inn [Ch. 12].','2009-06-17 20:11:41','2009-06-17 20:11:41'),(1420,'DRY0167',24,'Mowbray Ruined at Piquet','--- \n- \"478\"\n- \"33\"\n- \"298\"\n',222,165,6,'14.5 x 9.5','1894','1894',45,'vol. 17, facing p. 192','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts John Mowbray with a look combining anxiety and aggravation seated at the card table with Lord Etherington, who holds cards in his hands [Ch. 18].','2009-06-17 20:13:29','2009-06-17 20:13:29'),(1421,'DRY0168',24,'Mr. Cargill Accosting Lord Etherington','--- \n- \"173\"\n- \"175\"\n- \"395\"\n- \"478\"\n- \"34\"\n',222,165,6,'14.5 x 9.5','1894','1894',45,'vol. 17, facing p. 230','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts the Rev. Josiah Cargill confronting Lord Etherington, who is dressed in theatrical costume, in the grounds of Shaws Castle [Ch. 21].','2009-06-17 20:18:07','2009-06-17 20:18:07'),(1422,'DRY0169',24,'Mowbray and Clara','--- \n- \"177\"\n- \"298\"\n',222,165,6,'14.5 x 9.5','1894','1894',45,'vol. 17, facing p. 386','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts John Mowbray standing angrily over his sister, who reclines in alarm backwards on a sofa; an open box and assorted papers lie on the desk behind [Ch. 35].','2009-06-17 20:19:05','2009-06-17 20:19:05'),(1423,'DRY0170',24,'Death of Lord Etherington','--- \n- \"103\"\n- \"296\"\n- \"478\"\n- \"30\"\n- \"403\"\n- \"401\"\n',222,165,6,'14.7 x 9.5','1894','1894',45,'vol. 17, facing p. 426','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts the fallen body of Lord Etherington after the duel, held by his comrade Captain Jekyl, while Captain MacTurk peers downwards and Frank Tyrrel stands in his original position with a smoking pistol in hand [Ch. 39].','2009-06-17 20:20:57','2009-06-28 14:49:34'),(1424,'DRY0171',22,'Rachel Geddes 