er in a niche and enjoying each other’s company [Ch. 17].','2009-06-18 12:20:00','2009-06-18 12:20:00'),(1439,'DRY0186',4,'Archbishop Baldwin and De Lacy','--- \n- \"514\"\n- \"163\"\n- \"175\"\n- \"513\"\n',220,165,6,'9.1 x14.1','1894','1894',45,'vol. 19, facing p. 168','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Hugo de Lacy, standing before to the seated archprelate Baldwin, who wears ecclesiastical robes, and is listening to the chaplain reading from an illuminated volume [Ch. 18].','2009-06-18 12:24:58','2009-06-28 14:51:07'),(1440,'DRY0187',4,'Eveline Seized by the Welsh','--- \n- \"190\"\n- \"50\"\n- \"142\"\n',220,165,6,'14.2 x 9','1894','1894',45,'vol. 19, facing p. 220','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Eveline Berenger being seized by Welsh freebooters while out hunting [Ch. 23].','2009-06-18 12:26:25','2009-06-28 14:51:29'),(1441,'DRY0188',4,'Damian\'s Release','--- \n- \"330\"\n- \"513\"\n- \"85\"\n',220,165,6,'14.3 x 9.2','1894','1894',45,'vol. 19, facing p. 308','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Damian in prison having his fetters removed by the warder, while looking at the mysterious palmer there (actually his uncle Hugo in disguise). [Conclusion].','2009-06-18 12:28:13','2009-06-18 12:30:19'),(1442,'DRY0189',13,'Hamish Overcome by the Potion','--- \n- \"208\"\n- \"207\"\n- \"327\"\n',220,165,6,'14.5 x 9.4','1894','1894',45,'vol. 19, facing p. 430','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Hamish MacTavish succumbing to the effect of the sleeping potion administered by his mother, who looks on with hand on mouth [Ch. 11].\r\n\r\n','2009-06-18 12:29:48','2009-06-18 12:29:48'),(1443,'DRY0190',13,'Arrest of Hamish','--- \n- \"103\"\n- \"46\"\n- \"208\"\n- \"207\"\n- \"96\"\n',220,165,6,'14.4 x 9.2','1894\r\n','1894',45,'vol. 19, facing p. 444','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Hamish MacTavish, rifle in hand, with his mother standing in front of their hut, confronting three soldiers come to arrest him [Ch. 11].','2009-06-18 12:31:59','2009-06-18 12:31:59'),(1444,'DRY0191',26,'Richard and Sir Kenneth','--- \n- \"197\"\n- \"320\"\n- \"196\"\n- \"178\"\n',220,165,6,'14 x 9.5','1894','1894',45,'vol. 20 (frontispiece)','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts a bare-chested King Richard leaning upwards from his bed, and Kenneth standing in full armour (apart from helmet) before him [Ch. 15].\r\n\r\n','2009-06-18 12:33:50','2009-06-18 12:33:50'),(1445,'DRY0192',26,'Sir Kenneth and the Emir','--- \n- \"49\"\n- \"197\"\n- \"320\"\n- \"199\"\n',220,165,6,'8 x 5.5','1894','1894',45,'vol. 20 (title-page vignette)','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Kenneth and Saladin (as yet unknown to him) proceeding along together with their horses [Ch. 1].','2009-06-18 12:35:43','2009-06-18 12:35:43'),(1446,'DRY0193',26,'Sir Kenneth and the Hermit of Engaddi','--- \n- \"197\"\n- \"88\"\n- \"565\"\n',220,165,6,'14.9 x 9.5','1894','1894',45,'vol. 20, facing p. 44','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Kenneth and Theodorick kneeling in devotion inside the latter’s hermitage [Ch. 4].','2009-06-18 12:37:47','2009-06-18 12:37:47'),(1447,'DRY0194',26,'El Hakim Using the Talisman','--- \n- \"247\"\n- \"327\"\n- \"405\"\n- \"199\"\n- \"178\"\n- \"566\"\n',220,165,6,'15 x 9.5','1894','1894',45,'vol. 20, facing p. 90','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Saladin (as El Hakim) preparing a potion to administer to Kenneth’s sick squire, as Thomas de Multon (Lord of Gilsland) and the Archbishop of Tyre look on [Ch. 8].','2009-06-18 12:41:01','2009-06-18 12:41:01'),(1448,'DRY0195',26,'Richard Trampling on the Banner','--- \n- \"130\"\n- \"196\"\n',220,165,6,'14.7 x 9.4','1894','1894',45,'vol. 20, facing p. 126','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts King Richard trampling on the banner of Austria, before several onlookers, one of whom draws his sword [Ch.11].','2009-06-18 12:42:17','2009-06-18 12:42:17'),(1449,'DRY0196',26,'Berengaria Interceding for Sir Kenneth','--- \n- \"421\"\n- \"394\"\n- \"196\"\n- \"178\"\n',220,165,6,'9.4 x 14.5','1894','1894',45,'vol. 20, facing p. 172','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Queen Berengaria kneeling beside King Richard, who sits on his couch, and holding his hand, while Lady Edith stands further back in the pavilion [Ch. 17].','2009-06-18 12:44:19','2009-06-18 12:44:19'),(1450,'DRY0197',26,'The Nubian Stops the Assassin','--- \n- \"197\"\n- \"229\"\n- \"196\"\n',220,165,6,'14.6 x 9.4','1894','1894',45,'vol. 20, facing p. 220','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Sir Kenneth (disguised as Zohauk, a Nubian) dashing the Charegite assassin and his dagger to the ground, with King Richard glancing back to observe from his pavilion [Ch. 21].','2009-06-18 12:46:01','2009-06-18 12:46:01'),(1451,'DRY0198',26,'Conrad Detected by the Hound','--- \n- \"130\"\n- \"26\"\n- \"197\"\n- \"320\"\n- \"195\"\n- \"196\"\n- \"198\"\n',220,165,6,'14.4 x 9.1','1894','1894',45,'vol. 20, facing p. 252','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Conrade of Montserrat being held on the ground by Roswal, the hound of Sir Kenneth (himself disguised as a Nubian slave), as King Richard on horseback presides over the incident, with one more rider arriving, while other Christian Princes file past the banner in the distance [Ch. 24].\r\n\r\n','2009-06-18 12:47:58','2009-06-18 12:47:58'),(1452,'DRY0199',26,'Edith and Sir Kenneth','--- \n- \"130\"\n- \"155\"\n- \"197\"\n- \"394\"\n',220,165,6,'14.4 x 9.1','1894','1894',45,'vol. 20, facing p. 265','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Kenneth kneeling before Lady Edith in her pavilion, as she holds a candle and looks towards his face [Ch. 25].','2009-06-18 12:49:28','2009-06-18 12:49:28'),(1453,'DRY0200',26,'Saladin Slays the Grand Master','--- \n- \"567\"\n- \"103\"\n- \"247\"\n- \"222\"\n- \"199\"\n',220,165,6,'14.9 x 9.2','1894','1894',45,'vol. 20, facing p. 310','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Saladin in his tent with scimitar drawn behind his back ready to decapitate the Grand Master of the Templars, who also stands with his back to the viewer, with a goblet in hand [Ch. 28].','2009-06-18 12:51:48','2009-06-18 12:51:48'),(1454,'DRY0201',29,'Wildrake\'s Attempt to Assassinate Cromwell','--- \n- \"308\"\n- \"332\"\n- \"307\"\n- \"229\"\n- \"309\"\n',221,165,6,'14.6 x 9.5','1894','1894',45,'vol. 21 (frontispiece)','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Wildrake being disarmed held back by Markham Everard and Nehemiah Holdenough, after his bungled attempt kill Cromwell, who holds one hand within the buff jerkin which had resisted Wildrake’s sword [Ch. 30].','2009-06-18 12:53:57','2009-06-18 12:53:57'),(1455,'DRY0202',29,'Cromwell Apostrophising the Picture of Charles I','--- \n- \"172\"\n- \"308\"\n- \"309\"\n',221,165,6,'8 x 8','1894','1894',45,'vol. 21 (title-page vignette)','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Oliver Cromwell, in room with Roger Wildrake, standing before and pondering on a large portrait of Charles I standing up against the wall [Ch. 8]. Title/caption from List of Illustrations.','2009-06-18 12:55:32','2009-06-18 12:55:32'),(1456,'DRY0203',29,'Struggle Between Holdenough and Tomkins','--- \n- \"109\"\n- \"175\"\n- \"307\"\n- \"88\"\n- \"96\"\n- \"206\"\n',221,165,6,'14 x 9.5','1894','1894',45,'vol. 21, facing p. 6','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts the minister Holdenough frantically attempting to climb to the pulpit, with Tomkins holding his cloak and falling backwards having failed to stop him, with armed men also in the church [Ch. 1].','2009-06-18 13:01:40','2009-06-29 12:14:03'),(1457,'DRY0204',29,'The Fight Between Sir Henry Lee and Tomkins','--- \n- \"296\"\n- \"200\"\n- \"246\"\n- \"206\"\n',221,165,6,'9.5 x 14.5','1894','1894',45,'vol. 21, facing p. 24','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Sir Henry duelling in Woodstock Park with Joseph Tomkins, who adopts the guard position and wears a trooper’s helmet [Ch. 2].','2009-06-18 13:03:46','2009-06-18 13:03:46'),(1458,'DRY0205',1,'Everard Discovered in Joceline\'s Hut','--- \n- \"203\"\n- \"20\"\n- \"332\"\n- \"201\"\n- \"200\"\n- \"205\"\n',221,165,6,'14.5 x 9.5','1894','1894',45,'vol. 21, facing p. 48','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Sir Henry with cane in hand having burst into Joceline Joliffe’s cottage and finding there Markham Everard, who half kneels on the ground as Sir Henry holds him by the collar; Alice Lee with Phoebe Mayflower follows her father through the door [Ch. 4].','2009-06-18 13:06:06','2009-06-28 14:52:40'),(1459,'DRY0206',29,'Everard and Wildrake Riding to Joceline\'s Hut','--- \n- \"332\"\n- \"49\"\n- \"116\"\n- \"129\"\n- \"309\"\n',221,165,6,'15 x 9.5','1894','1894',45,'vol. 21, facing p. 144','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Markham Everard and Roger Wildrake riding at pace along a roadway through woods by moonlight [Ch. 13].','2009-06-18 13:08:09','2009-06-18 13:08:09'),(1460,'DRY0207',29,'Kerneguy Seized by Bevis','--- \n- \"203\"\n- \"319\"\n- \"26\"\n- \"479\"\n- \"520\"\n- \"200\"\n- \"129\"\n',221,165,6,'15 x 9.5','1894','1894',45,'vol. 21, facing p. 228','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Charles II (as Kerneguy) fallen below a window at Woodstock Lodge and held down by the hound Bevis, with Sir Henry at the window above holding a gun, and Joliffe running towards the scuffle with a cudgel, while Albert Lee holds his arm up towards the window [Ch. 19].','2009-06-18 13:10:28','2009-06-18 13:10:28'),(1461,'DRY0208',29,'Sir Henry Interrupts the Duel','--- \n- \"319\"\n- \"296\"\n- \"332\"\n- \"30\"\n- \"200\"\n',221,165,6,'9.7 x 14.5','1894','1894',45,'vol. 21, facing p. 296','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Sir Henry Lee arriving on horseback and commanding Markham Everard and Charles II to desist from their duel [Ch.25].','2009-06-18 13:12:14','2009-06-18 13:12:14'),(1462,'DRY0209',29,'Tomkins Killed by Jocelin Joliffe','--- \n- \"103\"\n- \"296\"\n- \"30\"\n- \"479\"\n- \"205\"\n- \"229\"\n- \"206\"\n',221,165,6,'14.2 x 9.4','1894','1894',45,'vol. 21, facing p. 362','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Joliffe with quarter-staff raised standing above the fallen body of Tomkins, who holds a fired pistol in one hand, as Phoebe Mayflower lying on the ground looks on with concern [Ch. 29].','2009-06-18 13:14:37','2009-06-18 13:14:37'),(1463,'DRY0210',29,'Cromwell\'s Entrance into Woostock Lodge','--- \n- \"308\"\n- \"201\"\n- \"200\"\n- \"96\"\n',221,165,6,'9.9 x 14.5','1894','1894',45,'vol. 21, facing p. 416','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Cromwell in uniform followed by a body of soldiers bursting in the hall at Woodstock Lodge, to be confronted by Sir Henry Lee, who stands with arms folded while his daughter watches on from behind; the contents of the hall lie around in disarray [Ch. 33].','2009-06-18 13:16:23','2009-06-18 13:16:23'),(1464,'DRY0211',9,'The Glee-Maiden','--- \n- \"26\"\n- \"524\"\n- \"74\"\n- \"84\"\n',223,165,6,'14.7 x 9.5','1894','1894',45,'vol. 22 (frontispiece)','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts The Glee Maiden Louise standing on some steps in a courtyard and playing her viol while a small dog lies beneath her; armed men can be seen coming out of the guarded archway opposite [Ch. 11].','2009-06-18 13:18:56','2009-06-29 12:27:22'),(1465,'DRY0212',9,'Catharine at Henry Smith\'s House','--- \n- \"225\"\n- \"210\"\n- \"209\"\n- \"339\"\n- \"178\"\n',223,165,6,'7 x 7','1894','1894',45,'vol. 22 (title-page vignette)','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Henry Gow placing Catharine Glover on a bed in a room with open window, and calling for the assistance of Luckie Shoolbred who stands in the doorway [Ch. 19]. Title/caption from List of Illustrations.','2009-06-18 13:21:25','2009-06-18 13:21:25'),(1466,'DRY0213',9,'Simon Glover and Catharine on the Way to Evening Service','--- \n- \"210\"\n- \"211\"\n- \"209\"\n- \"338\"\n- \"213\"\n',223,165,6,'9.5 x 14.6','1894','1894',45,'vol. 22, facing p. 8','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Simon Glover walking with stick along with his daughter Catharine through a street in Perth, followed by Conachar holding a staff at some distance; the figure by the side doffing his cap is presumably meant to represent Henry Gow [Ch. 2].','2009-06-18 13:23:13','2009-06-18 13:23:13'),(1467,'DRY0214',9,'The Kiss on St Valentine\'s Morn','--- \n- \"103\"\n- \"155\"\n- \"210\"\n- \"211\"\n- \"209\"\n- 