hilipson, seated before a table on which lies a coil of rope, facing the hooded Judges of the Secret Tribunal in a room lit by torches [Ch. 20].','2009-06-18 20:36:21','2009-06-18 20:36:21'),(1482,'DRY0229',2,'Arthur Philipson and Margaret of Anjou','--- \n- \"109\"\n- \"216\"\n- \"217\"\n',170,165,6,'14.4 x 9.4','1894','1894',45,'vol. 23, facing p. 304','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Arthur Philipson kneeling before Margaret of Anjou, as the widow of Henry VI, in the chapel Saint George in Strasburg Cathedral [Ch. 24].','2009-06-18 20:37:47','2009-06-18 20:37:47'),(1483,'DRY0230',2,'Finding the Body of the Duke of Burgundy','--- \n- \"323\"\n- \"467\"\n- \"320\"\n- \"217\"\n- \"406\"\n',170,165,6,'14.4 x 9.4','1894','1894',45,'vol. 23, facing p. 460','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Arthur Philipson and his father (as Earl of Oxford) finding the body of the Duke of Burgundy (along with that of Count Albert of Geierstein) on the battlefield [Ch. 36].','2009-06-18 20:39:35','2009-06-18 20:39:35'),(1484,'DRY0231',8,'Combat Between Count Robert and Hereward','--- \n- \"533\"\n- \"103\"\n- \"296\"\n- \"228\"\n- \"226\"\n',169,165,6,'14.5 x 9.4','1894','1894',45,'vol. 24 (frontispiece)','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Count Robert and Hereward in the lists axes raised ready to strike at each other, with other knights watching and Emperor Alexius mounted on his throne adjudicating [Ch. 34].','2009-06-18 20:41:39','2009-06-28 14:54:34'),(1485,'DRY0232',8,'Count Robert on the Emporer\'s Throne','--- \n- \"103\"\n- \"26\"\n- \"226\"\n',169,165,6,'7.2 x 6.5','1894','1894',45,'vol. 24 (title-page vignette)','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Count Robert of Paris seated on the Emperor’s throne, with wolf-hound at his side [Ch. 9]. Title/caption from List of Illustrations.','2009-06-18 20:42:55','2009-06-18 20:42:55'),(1486,'DRY0233',8,'Hereward and Sebastes of Mitylene','--- \n- \"103\"\n- \"228\"\n- \"229\"\n- \"227\"\n',169,165,6,'14.4 x 9.4','1894','1894',45,'vol. 24, facing p. 22','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Hereward striking away with his axe the dagger with which Sebastes of Mitylene, falling backwards, had attempted to assassinate him. [Ch. 2].\r\n\r\n','2009-06-18 20:44:28','2009-06-18 20:44:28'),(1487,'DRY0234',8,'Agelastes and Hereward','--- \n- \"408\"\n- \"34\"\n- \"228\"\n',169,165,6,'14.2 x 9.2','1894','1894',45,'vol. 24, facing p. 104','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Hereward having followed a path through woods and confronting the long-bearded Agelastes, who rises to greet him among the ruins [Chs 7 & 8].','2009-06-18 20:46:11','2009-06-18 20:46:11'),(1488,'DRY0235',8,'Count Robert and Brenhilda','--- \n- \"103\"\n- \"18\"\n- \"320\"\n- \"410\"\n- \"226\"\n',169,165,6,'14.5 x 9.4','1894','1894',45,'vol. 24, facing p. 178','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Count Robert and his wife Brenhilda in full dress, having prepared themselves to meet the Emperor; a long Norman shield is a prominent feature of the Count’s accoutrements [Ch. 14].','2009-06-18 20:48:44','2009-06-18 20:48:44'),(1489,'DRY0236',8,'Count Robert and Hereward in the Dungeons','--- \n- \"296\"\n- \"228\"\n- \"226\"\n- \"85\"\n',169,165,6,'9.4 x 14.5','1894','1894',45,'vol. 24, facing p. 204','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Count Robert and Hereward squaring up to each other in the dungeon, with the body of the jailer lying on the floor [Ch. 16].','2009-06-18 20:51:13','2009-06-28 14:55:10'),(1491,'DRY0238',8,'Tancred and the Crusaders','--- \n- \"103\"\n- \"49\"\n- \"320\"\n- \"572\"\n',169,165,6,'9.4 x 14.4','1894','1894',45,'vol. 24, facing p. 284','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Tancred with his accompanying Crusader knights proceeding from their encampment back toward Constantinople [Ch. 23].','2009-06-18 20:55:06','2009-06-18 20:57:20'),(1492,'DRY0239',8,'Death of Agelastes','--- \n- \"408\"\n- \"103\"\n- \"410\"\n- \"409\"\n',169,165,6,'14 x 9.2','1894','1894',45,'vol. 24, facing p. 300','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Agelastes being throttled by Sylvanus, the orang-utan, with a table falling behind him, while Brenhilda still looks on fearfully with a dagger in her hand [Ch. 26].','2009-06-18 20:56:32','2009-06-28 14:57:40'),(1493,'DRY0240',8,'The Emperor Visits Ursel','--- \n- \"533\"\n- \"535\"\n- \"85\"\n- \"536\"\n',169,165,6,'14.5 x 9.5','1894','1894',45,'vol. 24, facing p. 306','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Ursel lying in straw on the floor, with arm uplifted at the sound of the entry of Alexius Comnenus (torch in hand) and his daughter Anna Comnena into his cell [Ch. 27].','2009-06-18 20:59:00','2009-08-16 20:32:18'),(1494,'DRY0241',7,'Sir John de Walton Strikes Down Turnbull','--- \n- \"231\"\n- \"30\"\n- \"320\"\n- \"230\"\n- \"543\"\n',166,165,6,'14.3 x 9.3','1894','1894',45,'vol. 25 (frontispiece)','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Sir John de Walton in armour and with sword, having struck down Michael Turnbull, who lies on the ground as Lady Augusta intercedes [Ch. 17].','2009-06-19 08:15:27','2009-06-19 08:15:27'),(1495,'DRY0242',7,'Bertram the Minstrel and Lady Augusta of Berkley','--- \n- \"231\"\n- \"541\"\n- \"116\"\n',166,165,6,'14.3 x 9.3','1894','1894',45,'vol. 25 (title-page vignette)','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Bertram the minstrel accompanying Lady Augusta (in disguise) through the countryside [Ch. 1].\r\n','2009-06-19 08:19:53','2009-06-19 08:19:53'),(1496,'DRY0243',25,'Richard Middlemas\'s Farewell of Menie Gray','--- \n- \"155\"\n- \"236\"\n- \"573\"\n- \"336\"\n- \"75\"\n',170,165,6,'14.3 x 9.3','1894','1894',45,'vol. 25, facing p. 60','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Menie Gray embracing Richard Middlemas on his parting, with Nurse Jamieson weeping face in handkerchief on a bench in the room [Ch. 19].','2009-06-19 08:23:43','2009-06-19 08:23:43'),(1497,'DRY0244',25,'Death of Zilia Witherington','--- \n- \"336\"\n- \"232\"\n- \"178\"\n- \"574\"\n',170,165,6,'9.5 x 14.5','1894','1894',45,'vol. 25, facing p. 86','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts General Witherington arms upraised in fury, as his wife lies dead in the room, and facing Richard Middlamas, who backs off slightly though with a still haughty expression [Ch. 22].','2009-06-19 08:26:01','2009-06-19 08:27:41'),(1498,'DRY0245',25,'Richard Middlemas and Paupiah','--- \n- \"336\"\n- \"575\"\n',170,165,6,'14.2 x 9.2','1894','1894',45,'vol. 25, facing p. 194','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Middlemas disguised as ‘Sadoc’ standing in a darkened room before the seated Paupiah, who raises an admonishing finger [Ch. 26].','2009-06-19 08:29:55','2009-06-19 08:29:55'),(1499,'DRY0246',25,'Death of Richard Middlemas','--- \n- \"352\"\n- \"336\"\n- \"222\"\n',170,165,6,'14.3 x 9.4','1894','1894',45,'vol. 25, facing p. 146','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts a large elephant wrapping its trunk round the neck of Richard Middlemas, at the command of Hyder Ali [Ch. 28].','2009-06-19 08:31:57','2009-06-19 08:31:57'),(1500,'DRY0247',7,'Douglas Castle','--- \n- \"541\"\n- \"14\"\n- \"49\"\n- \"116\"\n- \"237\"\n',166,165,6,'14.6 x 9.3','1894','1894',45,'vol. 25, facing p. 206','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Sir Aymer de Valence and Bertram the minstrel, both on horseback, approaching Douglas Castle [Ch. 5].','2009-06-19 08:35:03','2009-06-19 08:35:03'),(1501,'DRY0248',7,'The Mysterious Knight (Sir James Douglas)','--- \n- \"544\"\n- \"49\"\n- \"320\"\n- \"354\"\n',166,165,6,'14.7 x 9.4','1894','1894',45,'vol. 25, facing p. 256','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Sir James Douglas mounted in full armour and holding lance in the town of Douglas, with Sir Aymer de Valence and his party visible at the far end of the street [Ch. 9].','2009-06-19 08:38:03','2009-06-19 08:38:03'),(1502,'DRY0249',7,'Lady August of Berkley and Sister Ursula','--- \n- \"231\"\n- \"542\"\n- \"219\"\n- \"288\"\n',166,165,6,'14.4 x 9.5','1894','1894',45,'vol. 25, facing p. 286','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts Lady Augusta and Sister Ursula converstion in St Bride’s Convent, with the former seated on a bed [Ch. 11].','2009-06-19 08:39:59','2009-06-19 08:39:59'),(1503,'DRY0250',7,'The Fight at the Church Interrupted','--- \n- \"323\"\n- \"109\"\n- \"320\"\n',166,165,6,'14.2 x 9.2','1894','1894',45,'vol. 25, facing p. 358','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts a cessation in hostilities between the English and Scottish knights, with the arrival of the Welshman Meredith, outside the church of Douglas [Ch. 20].','2009-06-19 08:41:32','2009-06-19 08:41:32'),(1504,'KEP0008',33,'The Lairds Jock','--- \n- \"103\"\n- \"576\"\n- \"296\"\n- \"178\"\n- \"96\"\n',25,47,3,'11.2 x 8.6','1828','1828',50,'facing p. 191','EUL, Corson E.KEE.1','0007409d.jpg#http://images.is.ed.ac.uk/luna/servlet/detail/UoEwal~1~1~53470~100079','Depicts the elderly John Armstrong (The Laird\'s Jock), standing loosely clad in his paid/blankets, with arm upraised in a posture of horror, his daughter clinging to his side; in the middle ground the English champion Foster stands over the body of the Laird\'s defeated son, holding aloft the two-handed sword he has gained in the combat, while assembled troops look on. Later published in H. I. and A. Stevens \'Scott and Scotland\' (London, 1845): see image.','2009-06-19 12:11:16','2009-09-11 10:04:12'),(1505,'DRY0237',8,'Brenhilda and Nicephorus Briennius','--- \n- \"571\"\n- \"410\"\n',169,165,6,'14.2 x 9.3','1894','1894',45,'vol. 24, facing p. 228','NLS, NG.1179.d','','Depicts the Caesar Nicephorus Briennius in conversation with the Countess Brenhilda, the latter holding her hand on the arm of her chair and with a defiant air [Ch. 18].','2009-06-28 15:51:08','2009-06-28 15:51:08'),(1506,'LAL0001',30,'','--- \n- \"103\"\n- \"109\"\n- \"256\"\n',224,194,7,'11 x 13','1829','1829',56,'[Plate 1]','NAL, 67.D.35','','Depicts a collection of images associated with Scott, including weaponry, a tartan, a sporran, and a large Highland hat, with (apparently) Melrose Abbey faintly visible in the background. ','2009-07-05 17:04:15','2009-08-16 20:33:28'),(1507,'LAL0002',23,'A Duel Between Frank and Rashleigh','--- \n- \"296\"\n- \"30\"\n- \"61\"\n- \"80\"\n- \"417\"\n',10,194,7,'10 x 13','1829','1829',56,'[Plate 5]','NAL, 67.D.35','','Depicts Frank and Rashleigh Osbaldistone duelling in a woodland setting, with Rob Roy interposing between them and attempting to hold them apart [Ch. 25]. Legend Dated 1 December 1828.','2009-07-05 17:11:50','2009-08-16 20:34:26'),(1508,'LAL0003',23,'Loch-Ard Scene of Morris\'s Drowning / (Rob Roy)','--- \n- \"143\"\n- \"46\"\n- \"124\"\n- \"370\"\n- \"72\"\n',224,194,7,'15.5 x 20.5','1829','1829',56,'[Plate 6]','NAL, 67.D.35','','Depicts a large group of Highlanders atop a cliff, with several peering over the edge to Loch Ard below, with ripples in the water suggesting that Morris has just fallen in [Ch. 31]. Legend dated 1 December 1828.','2009-07-05 17:14:35','2009-08-16 20:34:51'),(1509,'LAL0004',18,'Battle on Bothwell Bridge / (Old Mortality)','--- \n- \"103\"\n- \"323\"\n- \"243\"\n- \"49\"\n',224,194,7,'13.5 x 20.5','1829','1829',56,'[Plate 7]','NAL, 67.D.35','','Depicts the Battle of Bothwell Bridge, with combat occurring at one end of the bridge, with a cloud of smoke from an explosion obscuring the scene at the very centre [Ch. 32]. Legend dated 1 December 1828.','2009-07-05 17:16:25','2009-08-16 20:35:15'),(1510,'LAL0005',12,'Jeanny [sic] Deans Embarking for Rosneath / (Heart of Middle-Lothian)','--- \n- \"8\"\n- \"23\"\n- \"271\"\n- \"46\"\n- \"49\"\n- \"72\"\n- \"140\"\n',224,194,7,'15.5 x 21.5','1829','1829',56,'[Plate 8]','NAL, 67.D.35','','Depicts Jeanie Deans (whose back is to the viewer) standing on a shore near a moored boat, surrounded by a group of male figures in Highland dress, one of whom points towards the boat; a horse-drawn carriage is visible on the left, and a large mountain projecting from the sea forms the background; near the centre Dolly Dutton is being carried by two others to the boat [Ch. 42]. Legend dated 1 December 1828.','2009-07-05 17:18:51','2009-08-16 20:36:31'),(1511,'LAL0006',16,'The Escape from Argyle-Castle','--- \n- \"272\"\n- \"49\"\n- \"273\"\n- \"222\"\n',10,194,7,'14 x 16.5','1829','1829',56,'[Plate 9]','NAL, 67.D.35','','Depicts Dugald Dalgetty and Ranald MacEagh riding out of Inverary, the former with his hand on his forehead, the latter mounted and armed and looking backward, as they proceed away from a gallows, on which three figures have been hung, as two women weep below it [Ch. 14]. Legend dated 1 December 1828.','2009-07-05 17:20:16','2009-08-16 20:39:23'),(1512,'LAL0007',1,'Queen Mary at Loch-Leven Castle / (The Abbot)','--- \n- \"225\"\n- \"122\"\n',225,194,7,'12 x 18.5','1829','1829',56,'[Plate 10]','NAL, 67.D.35','','Depicts Mary Queen of Scots seated in her chamber at Loch Leven Castle, looking distraught, surrounded by four courtiers; one male courtier kneels at her feet, another stands behind bowing slightly, as the two women stand behind, one apparently weeping. Legend dated 1 December 1828. ','2009-07-05 17:21:39','2009-07-05 17:25:42'),(1513,'LAL0008',1,'A Fight in Higt [sic] Street Edinburgh/ (The Abbot)','--- \n- \"103\"\n- \"296\"\n- \"251\"\n- \"49\"\n- \"178\"\n',225,194,7,'13 x 18.5','1829','1829',56,'[Plate 11]','NAL, 67.D.35','','Depicts a fight between the Leslies and the Seytons in the High Street of Edinburgh, with one wounded figure lying on the ground next to a pistol, as another steps on his back, with St Giles Cathedral and possibly Edinburgh Castle faintly visible in the background to the right [Ch. 17]. Legend dated 1 December 1828.','2009-07-05 17:23:29','2009-08-16 20:40:40'),(1514,'LAL0009',13,'Hamish and his Mother / (Chronicles of the Canongate)','--- \n- \"20\"\n- \"46\"\n- \"208\"\n- \"207\"\n- \"146\"\n',224,194,7,'9.5 x 9.5','1829','1829',56,'[Plate 12]','NAL, 67.D.35','','Depicts Hamish MacTavish in full Highland dress standing and facing resolutely away from his mother’s cottage, as she crouches at his feet and holds his arm imploringly, attempting to pull him backward [Ch. 11]. Legend dated 1 December 1828.','2009-07-05 17:28:05','2009-08-16 20:41:02');
